1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:01,940
<i>Chief Igarashi!</i>

2
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:10,030
BOOMERANG DIVE

3
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:13,390
Mirage Step!

4
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:14,610
MIRAGE STEP

5
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,320
<i>Is that a Valkyrie skill?</i>

6
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:21,660
I-It hurts... I don't wanna die...

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:24,620
I can't stay in a messed-up 
place like this!

8
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:26,500
RETURN SCROLL: INSTANTLY EXIT A LABYRINTH.
REDUCES CONTRIBUTION POINTS WHEN USED. 
TARGET: USER AND HIS/HER PARTY

9
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,600
<i>She was left behind?!</i>

10
00:00:36,190 --> 00:00:40,190
<i>So she wasn't actually 
in a party with them?</i>

11
00:00:52,440 --> 00:01:03,080
THE WORLD'S STRONGEST REARGUARD

12
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:15,980
THE FIRST HURDLE

13
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:20,940
Run away, Chief! We'll take it from here!

14
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:22,420
Atobe-kun?

15
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:25,060
Don't worry about me! You two should run!

16
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:28,800
I can't afford to lose here!

17
00:02:33,920 --> 00:02:35,890
I'm the one you should be fighting!

18
00:02:36,230 --> 00:02:38,040
Thunderbolt!

19
00:02:38,110 --> 00:02:39,200
THUNDERBOLT

20
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:56,680
Is she already too low on power 
to activate Mirage Step?

21
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:03,890
Defense Support!

22
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:12,750
Defense Support!

23
00:03:14,580 --> 00:03:16,710
I-It worked that time?

24
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:21,960
That's right. Defense Support 
only works on party members!

25
00:03:24,230 --> 00:03:25,540
<i>If only...</i>

26
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:27,830
<i>I'd joined up with her then...</i>

27
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,500
Run...

28
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:34,870
Atobe-kun...

29
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:39,600
I'm sorry... I couldn't be of any use.

30
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:43,110
I'm the one who should apologize.

31
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:48,150
<i>I realized when Defense Support activated</i>

32
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:51,740
<i>that my skills can fully 
block that thing's attacks.</i>

33
00:03:51,830 --> 00:03:56,130
ATTACK SUPPORT LV. 1 ACQUIRED 
ADDS 10 INJURY POINTS TO ATTACKS
MADE BY PARTY MEMBERS IN FRONT

34
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:56,120
<i>If even that attack wasn't 
worth ten points...</i>

35
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:59,640
Theresia, I need your help!

36
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,210
I don't think so!

37
00:04:12,650 --> 00:04:14,940
<i>Even if my attacks don't land,</i>

38
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:19,900
<i>Theresia's attacks enhanced by my 
Attack Support can take you down!</i>

39
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,850
Theresia, I'll back you up!

40
00:04:38,960 --> 00:04:40,430
We beat it...

41
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:44,220
Chief Igarashi!

42
00:04:44,590 --> 00:04:47,530
Hey! You guys all right?

43
00:04:47,530 --> 00:04:50,430
Theresia, bring Ribault 
and his party here!

44
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:04,940
My level went up?

45
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,010
My skill points, too.

46
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:10,110
Good. Now I can get Recovery Support.

47
00:05:15,130 --> 00:05:18,430
Chief Igarashi, it's me, Atobe.

48
00:05:18,430 --> 00:05:20,480
Help is on the way,

49
00:05:20,480 --> 00:05:23,040
but I can give you first 
aid in the meantime.

50
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:26,260
Would you join my party so I can do that?

51
00:05:27,710 --> 00:05:32,320
If you... try anything 
funny... I'll sue you.

52
00:05:44,690 --> 00:05:45,650
DEFEATED MONSTER: REDFACE

53
00:05:49,180 --> 00:05:50,620
Wow, this looks bad.

54
00:05:50,620 --> 00:05:53,920
We're gonna get you to 
a Healer right away.

55
00:05:57,100 --> 00:05:59,130
What in the world happened?

56
00:06:01,490 --> 00:06:03,660
A Named monster showed up.

57
00:06:03,660 --> 00:06:06,250
It was close, but we 
managed to deal with it.

58
00:06:06,510 --> 00:06:10,550
A Named? You don't mean that 
red Cotton Ball, do you?

59
00:06:10,550 --> 00:06:14,350
That thing's capable of 
wiping out level 3 parties!

60
00:06:14,350 --> 00:06:16,290
How the hell did you—

61
00:06:16,850 --> 00:06:19,110
I'm sorry. That was rude of me.

62
00:06:19,110 --> 00:06:20,480
It's all right.

63
00:06:21,230 --> 00:06:24,520
My name's Elitia. What's yours?

64
00:06:24,810 --> 00:06:26,590
I'm Arihito.

65
00:06:26,590 --> 00:06:29,650
And you're... Suzuna-san, right?

66
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:31,000
Yes.

67
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:36,870
Um, didn't that woman they carried 
off reincarnate here when we did?

68
00:06:36,870 --> 00:06:39,600
Yeah, but don't worry.

69
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:42,570
She's unconscious, but 
her vitality has recovered.

70
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:43,680
Huh?

71
00:06:46,230 --> 00:06:48,290
Was there something you wanted to ask?

72
00:06:48,290 --> 00:06:50,620
N-No, nothing.

73
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:55,250
Of course. If there was a rearguard that 
talented around, it'd be a huge deal.

74
00:06:57,250 --> 00:07:01,010
<i>Elitia wanted to team up 
with a good rearguard.</i>

75
00:07:01,610 --> 00:07:04,370
<i>If I explain my job to her now,</i>

76
00:07:04,370 --> 00:07:07,110
<i>she might ask me to be in her party...</i>

77
00:07:07,110 --> 00:07:10,240
<i>but right now, the Chief's 
well-being comes first.</i>

78
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:13,890
Well, I'll be going.

79
00:07:13,890 --> 00:07:15,200
Oh... Right.

80
00:07:15,530 --> 00:07:17,830
We should go, too, Suzuna.

81
00:07:19,630 --> 00:07:20,810
See you around.

82
00:07:26,300 --> 00:07:29,990
It hasn't even been half a day, and 
you've been in a battle and made it back?

83
00:07:29,990 --> 00:07:31,340
Very heroic.

84
00:07:31,340 --> 00:07:34,940
Theresia, leave the weapon 
you used with the craftsman.

85
00:07:38,090 --> 00:07:41,650
Hm? Got something you want to tell me?

86
00:07:57,390 --> 00:08:00,870
Looks like she really 
took a liking to you.

87
00:08:00,870 --> 00:08:03,350
What? R-Really?

88
00:08:04,070 --> 00:08:10,420
Um, Leila-san, is there a way to 
officially add a mercenary to a party?

89
00:08:11,330 --> 00:08:12,720
You mean Theresia?

90
00:08:18,130 --> 00:08:20,180
A hundred Copper Tickets.

91
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,760
That's enough to buy a mercenary.

92
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:27,860
I normally only tell this to people 
who hire human mercenaries,

93
00:08:27,860 --> 00:08:30,570
but I think I'd like you to know.

94
00:08:31,470 --> 00:08:33,250
A hundred...

95
00:08:34,060 --> 00:08:38,440
<i>If that'll make her a member of my 
party, it doesn't seem too high.</i>

96
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:41,090
<i>We only went Seeking together once,</i>

97
00:08:41,090 --> 00:08:44,390
<i>but the teamwork I built up 
with her is indispensable.</i>

98
00:08:46,020 --> 00:08:47,540
Mr. Atobe!

99
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:50,660
You aren't hurt, are you? Or poisoned?

100
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:53,550
I'm unharmed, as you can see.

101
00:08:53,550 --> 00:08:55,130
What a relief!

102
00:08:57,040 --> 00:09:00,630
Louisa-san, could I talk 
to you for a moment?

103
00:09:01,200 --> 00:09:02,810
O-Of course...

104
00:09:05,060 --> 00:09:07,820
The results of this Seeking...

105
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:10,690
You slew Redface, a monster 
carrying a bounty.

106
00:09:10,690 --> 00:09:12,900
The reward for that is 20 gold coins.

107
00:09:12,900 --> 00:09:14,830
And your Contribution Points total...

108
00:09:14,830 --> 00:09:17,030
280?!

109
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:19,290
That's amazing! Too amazing!

110
00:09:19,290 --> 00:09:22,960
The most Contribution Points I 
ever earned as a Seeker was 105!

111
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:27,860
And I had to kill 50 Cotton 
Balls just to reach level 2!

112
00:09:28,160 --> 00:09:32,370
Louisa-san, what's the "Trust" 
that's displayed there?

113
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:37,810
In the guild, whether or not one builds 
harmonious relationships with other Seekers

114
00:09:37,810 --> 00:09:40,250
is reflected in your Contribution Points.

115
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:41,430
Huh...

116
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:46,440
Of course, Trust is normally something 
that can't be quantified,

117
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:51,190
but your license rates and quantifies it 
based on the condition of your partymates.

118
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:56,100
Your Trust increase rate 
also affects your Contribution Points.

119
00:09:56,380 --> 00:10:01,020
But it rarely goes any higher than 
five at best in a single Seeking...

120
00:10:02,350 --> 00:10:04,340
And yet you have 50?!

121
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:08,030
Just how close did you two 
get in such a short time?!

122
00:10:08,030 --> 00:10:10,190
This is an incredible number!

123
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:14,450
<i>I see... So is that why...</i>

124
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:17,240
<i>Theresia acted like that earlier?</i>

125
00:10:18,140 --> 00:10:20,950
<i>To make the most of my 
strengths as a Rearguard,</i>

126
00:10:20,950 --> 00:10:24,070
<i>I need good relationships with 
my vanguard and midguard.</i>

127
00:10:24,070 --> 00:10:26,940
<i>In other words, as we 
all support each other,</i>

128
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:30,390
<i>they'll grow fond of me 
to an abnormal degree?</i>

129
00:10:30,390 --> 00:10:33,860
<i>What?! Wait, isn't that really bad?</i>

130
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:38,490
Trust doesn't usually go up with 
a demi-human, and yet yours...

131
00:10:38,850 --> 00:10:42,810
This might make your new and unknown job

132
00:10:42,810 --> 00:10:46,570
the most powerful rearguard 
job in the world!

133
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,470
Huh? Oh, no, I don't think...

134
00:10:49,970 --> 00:10:53,110
Oh... Also, Louisa-san,

135
00:10:53,110 --> 00:10:56,260
please don't tell anyone 
about this just yet.

136
00:10:56,260 --> 00:10:58,730
Right... I see.

137
00:10:58,730 --> 00:11:01,140
If word of your achievement gets out,

138
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:04,470
a lot of people might come around 
who just want to use you.

139
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,220
I understand.

140
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:08,250
Thank you.

141
00:11:08,250 --> 00:11:09,680
At any rate,

142
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:23,610
CURRENT RANKING 
OVERALL: 137529/139444 
DISTRICT 8: 1124/3039

143
00:11:09,680 --> 00:11:15,000
you currently rank 137,529th overall,

144
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,110
and 1,124th in District 8 alone.

145
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:21,400
There are around 3,000 
Seekers in District 8,

146
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,640
so that puts you in the top half.

147
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:28,070
That qualifies you for lodging 
in a suite in District 8.

148
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:30,160
A suite?

149
00:11:31,010 --> 00:11:37,000
Also, the one who was brought to 
the Healer, Ms. Kyouka Igarashi...

150
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,390
I'm told she has awakened 
in the emergency room.

151
00:11:44,450 --> 00:11:45,770
Pardon me.

152
00:11:47,430 --> 00:11:50,360
Thank goodness. I didn't know 
what might happen to you.

153
00:11:50,670 --> 00:11:53,790
I thought I was a goner for sure.

154
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:56,710
Thank you for saving me, Atobe-kun.

155
00:11:57,690 --> 00:12:01,180
When people find out 
you defeated a Named,

156
00:12:01,180 --> 00:12:05,130
you'll probably have a lot of high-ranked 
parties fighting over you.

157
00:12:05,130 --> 00:12:07,210
You shot up the ranks quick.

158
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:10,960
Me, on the other hand...

159
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:14,330
I was KO'd and had to be 
rescued by supporters.

160
00:12:14,330 --> 00:12:15,920
Zero Contribution Points.

161
00:12:18,180 --> 00:12:20,680
I just picked a job that sounded cool

162
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,860
and couldn't find any partymates.

163
00:12:22,860 --> 00:12:27,520
I thought I could manage on my 
own, but I couldn't at all.

164
00:12:28,350 --> 00:12:33,590
I thought you were very cool when you 
saw me in danger and didn't run away.

165
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:38,140
That ended up motivating me.

166
00:12:38,140 --> 00:12:43,000
Though I'm sure it was pure luck 
that I was able to kill that thing.

167
00:12:44,610 --> 00:12:46,820
Anyway, Chief...

168
00:12:47,290 --> 00:12:51,380
could I convince you to 
officially join my party?

169
00:12:52,210 --> 00:12:55,610
If you decide I'm worth teaming up with,

170
00:12:55,610 --> 00:12:58,440
you're free to leave then and there.

171
00:12:58,440 --> 00:13:01,290
I will do the best I can, but...

172
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:09,260
You saved me, and then you comforted me.

173
00:13:09,450 --> 00:13:12,760
I'm not the kind of loser

174
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:17,140
who'd refuse to do what 
you ask after all that.

175
00:13:17,470 --> 00:13:22,440
U-Um... Can I take that 
to mean you accept?

176
00:13:25,290 --> 00:13:28,530
Th-Thank you! In that case, Chief—

177
00:13:28,530 --> 00:13:29,960
A-Atobe-kun...

178
00:13:31,150 --> 00:13:34,620
Could you call me something 
other than "Chief"?

179
00:13:35,020 --> 00:13:35,920
Huh?

180
00:13:36,850 --> 00:13:40,500
Th-Then... Igarashi-san?

181
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,710
That feels kinda weird...

182
00:13:42,710 --> 00:13:45,800
but I look forward to working with you.

183
00:13:49,970 --> 00:13:54,970
THE WORLD'S STRONGEST REARGUARD

184
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:54,550
Any good rearguards around here-guard?

185
00:13:54,970 --> 00:13:59,980
THE WORLD'S STRONGEST REARGUARD

186
00:13:56,790 --> 00:13:59,160
This feels like a shampoo commercial!

187
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:02,990
Are you sure about this?

188
00:14:02,990 --> 00:14:06,420
You really don't mind me 
staying at your place?

189
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:07,600
Of course not.

190
00:14:07,600 --> 00:14:10,360
Then I guess I'll take you up on that.

191
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:15,800
Want to stop by here first?

192
00:14:16,040 --> 00:14:17,470
Can we?

193
00:14:21,970 --> 00:14:24,420
You wear clothes like that, too?

194
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:28,460
Oh, I mean... I've only ever 
seen you in suits and such.

195
00:14:28,460 --> 00:14:30,340
Yeah, I guess so.

196
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:32,890
And we never really met 
outside the office.

197
00:14:32,890 --> 00:14:36,970
Yeah, and we never went 
drinking or anything, either.

198
00:14:36,970 --> 00:14:42,360
In fact, I don't think I ever spoke with 
you about anything other than work.

199
00:14:43,130 --> 00:14:45,640
This is kind of embarrassing, but...

200
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:50,270
I had a curfew.

201
00:14:50,620 --> 00:14:53,470
I always had to be home before then.

202
00:14:53,470 --> 00:14:55,320
Oh, I had no idea.

203
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:59,050
I thought it was silly, 
since I'm an adult now,

204
00:14:59,050 --> 00:15:02,210
but since my parents always 
decided everything in my life,

205
00:15:02,210 --> 00:15:03,790
I couldn't manage alone.

206
00:15:04,310 --> 00:15:09,700
And then I got a marriage offer 
from one of my dad's clients.

207
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:11,450
M-Marriage?

208
00:15:11,450 --> 00:15:13,450
Selfish, right?

209
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:17,210
But at the time, I finally 
realized deep down

210
00:15:17,210 --> 00:15:19,130
that I couldn't keep living like that.

211
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:22,120
So I built up my career 
and struck out on my own.

212
00:15:22,120 --> 00:15:24,980
I worked frantically every day to 
reach a point where my parents

213
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:26,900
wouldn't have a say anymore.

214
00:15:33,770 --> 00:15:36,790
I made so many unreasonable 
demands of you.

215
00:15:36,790 --> 00:15:38,030
I'm sorry.

216
00:15:38,030 --> 00:15:39,310
Not at all.

217
00:15:40,300 --> 00:15:45,230
<i>I guess she just wanted to protect 
her own life, in her own way.</i>

218
00:15:45,860 --> 00:15:50,000
I'm glad I got to know 
you a little better.

219
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,170
Huh?

220
00:15:51,490 --> 00:15:54,950
We're going to be a party 
from now on, after all.

221
00:15:54,950 --> 00:15:56,390
That's true.

222
00:15:56,390 --> 00:15:59,120
Well, let's eat before it gets cold.

223
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,880
Hey, did you hear?

224
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,750
Apparently Death Sword's 
back in District 8.

225
00:16:04,060 --> 00:16:06,540
Oh, you mean Elitia?

226
00:16:07,020 --> 00:16:09,230
I heard she's snapped up a novice

227
00:16:09,230 --> 00:16:11,850
to try to raise her until 
she amounts to something.

228
00:16:11,850 --> 00:16:14,980
<i>They're talking about Elitia and Suzuna?</i>

229
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:18,830
She ran all the way here after 
leaving the White Night Brigade?

230
00:16:20,790 --> 00:16:22,880
Shouldn't we see this as an opportunity?

231
00:16:22,880 --> 00:16:25,520
A high-ranked Seeker carrying 
that kinda baggage around?

232
00:16:25,520 --> 00:16:26,760
If we play it right...

233
00:16:26,760 --> 00:16:29,310
Hey. Save that for later.

234
00:16:34,790 --> 00:16:36,930
W-Well, then...

235
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:43,120
Goodnight.

236
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:46,170
Yes, goodnight.

237
00:16:50,870 --> 00:16:55,280
H-Hey, Atobe-kun... Could I...

238
00:16:57,950 --> 00:17:01,710
Igarashi-san? What's the matter?

239
00:17:01,710 --> 00:17:06,770
Well, how do I put this? Please 
don't think badly of me, but...

240
00:17:06,770 --> 00:17:10,120
I'd prefer it if you slept 
with your back to me...

241
00:17:10,460 --> 00:17:13,920
O-Oh... I guess I turned 
over in my sleep.

242
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:16,560
I know you can't help that...

243
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:21,330
but when you sleep facing me, I 
just... can't help noticing...

244
00:17:21,330 --> 00:17:24,020
Even I think it's weird, but...

245
00:17:27,010 --> 00:17:27,890
<i>Hang on.</i>

246
00:17:29,310 --> 00:17:31,320
RECOVERY SUPPORT LV. 1

247
00:17:31,660 --> 00:17:34,850
<i>The Rearguard skill Recovery Support 1!</i>

248
00:17:34,850 --> 00:17:38,780
<i>That's right! In this position, 
we're vanguard and rearguard!</i>

249
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:44,840
I-I-I'm so sorry! I'll 
sleep in the living room!

250
00:17:44,840 --> 00:17:45,620
Huh?

251
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:50,000
RECOVERY SUPPORT LV. 1

252
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:55,130
<i>Recovery Support 1 stays in 
effect even outside of combat?</i>

253
00:17:55,130 --> 00:17:58,540
<i>I'll have to move my bed tomorrow.</i>

254
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:05,590
So, um...

255
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:08,580
Sorry I haven't introduced myself yet.

256
00:18:08,580 --> 00:18:10,790
I'm Kyouka Igarashi.

257
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:14,380
Thanks for saving me 
yesterday, Theresia-san.

258
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:18,980
Did I do something bad?

259
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:23,830
No, it's not that at all. 
Don't worry about it.

260
00:18:25,930 --> 00:18:27,360
Excuse me.

261
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:31,500
I'm here about the monster dissection 
and armor work that I requested.

262
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:39,470
<i>Theresia got a Red Buckler 
that reduces fire damage,</i>

263
00:18:39,470 --> 00:18:43,100
<i>Igarashi-san got a scarf 
that reduces fire damage,</i>

264
00:18:43,430 --> 00:18:47,090
<i>and I got my slingshot 
turned into a Blaze Shot.</i>

265
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:49,380
We made it in time.

266
00:18:49,380 --> 00:18:54,070
Good thing we left the materials from the 
Redface with that dissector yesterday.

267
00:18:54,910 --> 00:19:00,020
Now that we have these items, I'll 
have you two be my vanguard today.

268
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:05,190
Igarashi-san, I'll back you up!

269
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:14,030
Defense Support!

270
00:19:15,030 --> 00:19:18,000
<i>Good. My support reaches 
everyone serving as vanguard.</i>

271
00:19:23,050 --> 00:19:26,470
DEFEATED MONSTERS 
COTTON BALL: 15   POISON SPEAR BEE: 3

272
00:19:27,530 --> 00:19:30,720
So if we go through there, 
we'll be on the second floor?

273
00:19:31,150 --> 00:19:33,110
It feels kinda creepy.

274
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:39,910
<i>To get the 100 tickets needed 
to add Theresia to the party ASAP,</i>

275
00:19:39,910 --> 00:19:43,300
<i>we should probably fight some stronger 
monsters on the second floor.</i>

276
00:19:43,830 --> 00:19:45,150
<i>But...</i>

277
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:53,790
JUGGERNAUT

278
00:19:45,150 --> 00:19:48,870
<i>there are rumors that a Named 
has been showing up there.</i>

279
00:19:48,870 --> 00:19:53,430
<i>One vicious enough to take 
out level 3 and 4 parties.</i>

280
00:19:55,350 --> 00:19:57,580
<i>We're still only level 2.</i>

281
00:19:57,580 --> 00:20:00,690
<i>If we run into a monster 
like that, we're done for.</i>

282
00:20:01,960 --> 00:20:05,730
Theresia, Igarashi-san, 
let's head back for toda—

283
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:10,070
<i>Was that voice...</i>

284
00:20:11,430 --> 00:20:12,970
We don't have a choice now!

285
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:22,870
Elitia?

286
00:20:22,870 --> 00:20:24,300
Suzuna?

287
00:20:26,420 --> 00:20:27,610
And they're up against...

288
00:20:28,990 --> 00:20:30,870
FANGED ORC

289
00:20:29,030 --> 00:20:30,530
a Fanged Orc?

290
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,790
Suzuna, stay back!

291
00:20:32,790 --> 00:20:34,200
Slash Ripper!

292
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,830
SLASH RIPPER

293
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:43,770
Igarashi-san, Theresia!

294
00:20:43,770 --> 00:20:46,010
We'll draw the bees' attention to us!

295
00:20:46,010 --> 00:20:47,050
Got it!

296
00:20:47,780 --> 00:20:48,370
ACCEL DASH

297
00:20:50,750 --> 00:20:51,840
Arihito-san!

298
00:20:56,650 --> 00:20:58,310
They're too far away!

299
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,480
Defense Support!

300
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:08,290
Thunderbolt!

301
00:21:14,790 --> 00:21:16,050
Are you all right?

302
00:21:16,460 --> 00:21:19,630
Y-Yes... I'm fine.

303
00:21:19,630 --> 00:21:23,650
But I know I'm just holding her back.

304
00:21:24,040 --> 00:21:25,770
No, you're not.

305
00:21:25,770 --> 00:21:29,750
You made it this far, and even 
defeated all those Cotton Balls.

306
00:21:30,050 --> 00:21:31,610
Oh, I get it.

307
00:21:31,610 --> 00:21:34,790
To help Suzuna level up more efficiently,

308
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:38,180
you broke up your party so 
you can draw enemies to you

309
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:40,570
and let Suzuna deal the finishing blow.

310
00:21:40,570 --> 00:21:41,460
Yes.

311
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:45,470
But those bees attack 
rearguards like Suzuna, too.

312
00:21:45,470 --> 00:21:49,080
Wouldn't it be safer to look 
for other monsters to fight?

313
00:21:49,330 --> 00:21:51,380
We don't have time for that.

314
00:21:51,380 --> 00:21:55,620
I need to get Suzuna as strong as 
I am quickly and get back there.

315
00:21:56,560 --> 00:21:57,590
"Back there"?

316
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:03,380
Do you mean—and I'm 
sorry if I'm wrong—

317
00:22:03,380 --> 00:22:04,760
back to the White Night Brigade?

